<report>
<title>Woolf chi-square analysis of 2 by 2 series</title>
<block name="table">

<p><u>For table <in>table</in></u><br />
Percentages:  A = <in>pc_a</in> C = <in>pc_c</in> Total = <in>pc_t</in></p>
<block name="warn_small"><p><warn>WARNING: SMALL EXPECTED FREQUENCIES, CHECK BY EXACT METHODS</warn></p></block>
<p>Uncorrected Chi&#xb2; = <in>table_chi_2</in> Chi = <in>table_chi</in><br />
Yates' corrected Chi&#xb2; = <in>yates_chi_2</in> Chi = <in>yates_chi</in> <pval><inp>yates_chi_p</inp></pval></p>

<block name="no_haldane">
<p><b>Without Haldane Correction:</b><br />
Odds ratio = <in>odds</in>  log odds ratio = <in>log</in><br />
Variance of log odds ratio = <in>var</in>  standard error = <in>se</in>  weight = <in>weight</in><br />
Chi&#xb2; = <in>chi_2</in> Chi = <in>chi</in><ci> </ci><pval><inp>chi_p</inp></pval><br />
<ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% CI for log odds ratio = <in>ci_from</in> to <in>ci_to</in></ci><br />
<ci>Giving an odds ratio of <in>odds_from</in> to <in>odds_to</in></ci></p></block>
<block name="warn_no_haldane">
<p><warn>ODDS RATIO NOT COMPUTABLE WITHOUT HALDANE CORRECTION</warn></p>
</block>
<block name="haldane">

<p><b>With Haldane Correction:</b><br />
Odds ratio = <in>odds</in>  log odds ratio = <in>log</in><br />
Variance of log odds ratio = <in>var</in>  standard error = <in>se</in>  weight = <in>weight</in><br />
Chi&#xb2; = <in>chi_2</in>  Chi = <in>chi</in> <pval><inp>chi_p</inp></pval><br />
<ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% CI for log odds ratio = <in>ci_from</in> to <in>ci_to</in></ci><br />
<ci>Giving an odds ratio of <in>odds_from</in> to <in>odds_to</in></ci></p>
</block>
</block>
<br />
<block name="combined_no_haldane">
<p><b>For combined tables without Haldane correction:</b><br />
Number of Tables = <in>tables</in><br />
Mean log odds ratio = <in>mean</in> giving odds ratio = <in>odds</in><br />
Variance of mean log odds ratio = <in>var</in>  standard error = <in>se</in><br />
<ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% CI for mean log odds ratio = <in>ci_from</in> to <in>ci_to</in></ci><br />
<ci>Giving odds ratio of <in>odds_from</in> to <in>odds_to</in></ci><br />
Chi&#xb2; for expected log odds ratio = 0 is <in>chi_2</in> Chi = <in>chi</in> <pval><inp>chi_p</inp></pval><br />
Chi&#xb2; for heterogeneity = <in>het_chi_2</in> DF = <in>df</in> <pval><inp>het_chi_p</inp></pval></p>
</block>
<block name="combined_with_haldane">

<p><b>For combined tables with Haldane correction:</b><br />
Number of tables = <in>tablesx</in><br />
Mean log odds ratio = <in>meanx</in> giving odds ratio = <in>oddsx</in><br />
Variance of mean log odds ratio = <in>varx</in>  standard error = <in>sex</in><br />
<ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% CI for mean log odds ratio = <in>ci_fromx</in> to <in>ci_tox</in></ci><br />
<ci>Giving odds ratio of <in>odds_fromx</in> to <in>odds_tox</in></ci><br />
Chi&#xb2; for expected log odds ratio = 0 is <in>chi_2x</in> Chi = <in>chix</in> <pval><inp>chi_px</inp></pval><br />
Chi&#xb2; for heterogeneity = <in>het_chi_2x</in> DF = <in>dfx</in> <pval><inp>het_chi_px</inp></pval></p>
</block>
</report>
